# D:\Work\Fut\.gitignore
#
# WHAT IS EXCLUDED AND WHY
#
# This repository holds the SOURCE and the DOCUMENTATION of the Calabiyau
# (Strinova) UE 4.25 reverse-engineering work, not the multi-hundred-megabyte
# reverse-engineering scratch that produced it. The excluded items are either
# reproducible, machine-specific, or far past GitHub's practical limits.

# ---- IDA databases (295 MB + 236 MB single files; GitHub caps at 100 MB) ----
# The ACE-Base64.dll database is regenerable from the DLL. Keeping it in git
# would also make every clone 600 MB for no benefit.
ida/*.id0
ida/*.id1
ida/*.id2
ida/*.nam
ida/*.til
ida/*.idb

# ---- compiler / linker intermediates ----
# .iobj/.ipdb are MSVC incremental-link state: large, machine-specific, and
# regenerated by the next build.
*.obj
*.iobj
*.ipdb
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.exp
*.lib
!cheat/loader/zlibwapi_orig.lib
*.log
*.tlog

# ---- built binaries ----
# The deliverable DLLs are produced by `tools/build_protected.ps1`; committing
# them would put a moving, hash-checked artifact in history for no gain.
cheat/build/
out/
*.dll
*.exe
!inject/**/*.exe

# ---- Dumper-7 third-party checkout ----
# Upstream project, vendored only to build the dumper. Fetch with git, do not
# re-host.
dumper/src/Dumper-7-main/

# ---- session recordings ----
# These are THIS PROJECT'S OWN agent session transcripts: tens of megabytes of
# JSONL plus screenshots. They contain no source value and would dominate the
# repository size.
dsh-session-*/
zcode-migrate/

# ---- misc machine state ----
*.suo
*.user
.vs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
